--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SCOPE / DELIVERABLE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Native SwiftUI parity of the DriveDetailPage orchestration shell. The web page
loads one drive (useDriveDetailData(id) -> useDrive + useVehicle), derives the
per-drive stats every sub-panel reads, and renders each section wrapped in its
own SectionErrorBoundary. The manifest scopes this unit to requiredCount=25
(states 2 + strings 23); the page's charts/panels/map are not separate manifest
units, so they are reproduced natively in-place (Swift Charts / MapKit wrappers,
never WKWebView) without inflating the parity count.

Implemented files (apps/apple/Sources/Features/Driving/**):
  DriveDetailModels.swift            value types + DriveDetailSection catalog (19 fallback keys)
  DriveDetailStats.swift             pure DriveStats.compute (web stats useMemo + speedHistData)
  DriveDetailFormat.swift            SI -> display formatters (web fmtNumber/convert*FromSI + '—')
  DriveDetailPageModel.swift         @Observable model; loading/error/ready; data-source seam
  DriveDetailPageModel.Sample.swift  Sample/Empty/Failing data sources
  DriveDetailComponents.swift        section error-boundary, glass section card, metric grid,
                                     skeleton (redacted), no-telemetry banner
  DriveDetailHeaderSection.swift     header (title/vehicle/date + Replay/Share)
  DriveDetailSummarySections.swift   hero gauges, timeline, stat cards
  DriveDetailDetailSections.swift    more-details, energy summary, journey details
  DriveDetailCostSection.swift       cost & savings (documented default rates, surfaced in caption)
  DriveDetailChartSections.swift     overview/SOC/elevation/temperature/power (Swift Charts)
  DriveDetailMapSection.swift        route map (TSMapView / MapKit)
  DriveDetailDiagnosticSections.swift speed histogram, tyre pressure, why-ended, Helix insights x2
  DriveDetailPage.swift              top-level adaptive View; phase switch; all sections in web order
  DriveDetailRouteRegistration.swift DriveDetailLink + .driveDetailDestination() + make() (sub-route)
Tests:
  apps/apple/Tests/Unit/Features/Driving/DriveDetailPageModelTests.swift  (21 cases)
Strings:
  apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings  (+91 driveDetail.* keys; the 23 required + labels)

