PRE-EXISTING / OUT-OF-SCOPE ISOLATIONS (build overrides only — NO source edits)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The available runner ships Xcode 26.5 / Swift 6.3, newer than the repo's pinned
toolchain (apps/macos-pending-verifications.md). Two PRE-EXISTING, repo-wide,
out-of-scope defect classes (identical for all 56 sibling page rows; none in the
Features/Driving allowed scope; my 14 sources + test produce ZERO diagnostics):

  A) DEBUG-only #Preview ViewBuilder errors — 25 *.Previews.swift files use an
     explicit `return` inside a `#Preview` ViewBuilder, which 26.5 rejects
     ("cannot use explicit 'return' statement in the body of result builder
     'ViewBuilder'"), e.g. TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/Input.Previews.swift.
     All are `#if DEBUG`-guarded preview canvases (not shipped surface code).
     Isolated via EXCLUDED_SOURCE_FILE_NAMES=*.Previews.swift.
  B) Pre-existing broken test files unrelated to this page:
     AlertStudioPage.Tests.swift / AlertStudioPage.ViewModelTests.swift
       ("cannot find 'AlertStudioSamples' in scope") and
     GDPRExportPageModelTests.swift (main-actor isolation, per SleepEfficiency log).
     For this page's run the test target compiles ONLY this page's test file via
     INCLUDED_SOURCE_FILE_NAMES (an Xcode build override, no source edits).
  Release-config note: a swift-frontend SIL optimizer crash (CopyPropagation) on the
  pre-existing TeslaSync.LayoutSwitcherLoaded.init function aborts -configuration
  Release whole-module optimization. Debug (no SIL opt) builds clean; this page's
  code is not in the crash. Documented as an environment/toolchain defect.

These isolations are command-line build settings only; no out-of-scope file was
edited (mirrors the accepted Powershare/SleepEfficiency P7 methodology). Fixing
them would breach this artifact's allowed-files scope.

